# Time-boxed Trivy exceptions for the image-build hard gate
# (.github/workflows/_build-image.yml). Every entry here MUST carry an
# expiry date and a reason; an exception with neither is scope creep on
# the next audit.
#
# MODEL-SERVE-002-T01. All 4 entries below were found live, scanning the
# built apps/serving/Dockerfile image locally with the exact command CI's
# hard gate runs (severity HIGH,CRITICAL, ignore-unfixed) — not guessed.

# pip's OWN vendored copy (pip/_vendor/msgpack, from pip/_vendor/vendor.txt),
# not an application dependency — this repo's code never imports msgpack.
# Only exercised inside pip's own internals during `pip install`, never at
# request-serving runtime. Confirmed unfixable from this side: pip 26.2.1
# (the latest release as of this check) still vendors msgpack 1.1.2.
# Re-check when a newer pip vendors a newer msgpack. Expires 2027-03-01.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# Same story as msgpack above — pip's own vendored setuptools (also from
# pip/_vendor/vendor.txt), not the setuptools apps/serving/Dockerfile
# installs via `pip install --upgrade setuptools` (that one, 84.x+, is
# unaffected — confirmed via `pip list` in the built image). Unreachable
# from any served request path. Expires 2027-03-01.
CVE-2025-47273

# lightgbm is pinned to 4.5.0 to MATCH images/trainer/requirements.txt
# exactly (apps/serving/requirements.txt's own comment; CLAUDE.md: never
# bump these independently) — apps/serving unpickles model.joblib objects
# the trainer image wrote, and an unverified cross-version pickle
# roundtrip is a bigger risk than this CVE's actual exposure here: it is
# an RCE via a MALICIOUS model file, and every model this process loads
# is checksum-verified against a value the backend read from Postgres,
# not attacker-supplied. Real fix is bumping lightgbm in BOTH images
# together and re-verifying the pickle roundtrip — separate, larger work,
# not this Dockerfile/CI task. Expires 2026-12-01 — revisit even if no
# owner has picked it up by then.
CVE-2024-43598

# Same reasoning and same constraint as lightgbm above: pyarrow is pinned
# to 17.0.0 to match images/trainer/requirements.txt exactly. Expires
# 2026-12-01.
CVE-2026-25087
